verses.tf_en:
① **«زَعَمَ الَّذِیْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنْ لَّنْ یُّبْعَثُوْا»** (The disbelievers alleged that they will surely not be raised again;) — The hardened disbelievers boastfully and erroneously assert that they shall never be resurrected once their bones have decayed and turned to dust in the earth;
② **«قُلْ بَلٰی وَرَبِّیْ لَتُبْعَثُنَّ ثُمَّ لَتُنَبَّؤُنَّ بِمَا عَمِلْتُمْ»** (Proclaim (O dear Prophet Mohammed – peace and blessings be upon him), “Surely yes, why not? By oath of Lord, you will surely be raised again and you will then be informed of your misdeeds;) — Proclaim with unshakeable certainty, O Beloved Messenger ﷺ: 'Nay, by the solemn oath of my Cherishing Lord! You shall most definitely be resurrected from your graves, and then every single deed, word, and transgression you committed shall be laid bare and declared unto you!';
③ **«وَذٰلِكَ عَلَی اللّٰهِ یَسِیْرٌ»** (And this is easy for Allah.”) — And resurrecting all generations of humanity simultaneously and bringing them to exact account is effortless, simple, and easy for the infinite omnipotence of Allah!

verses.tf_bn:
① **«یَوْمَ یَجْمَعُكُمْ لِیَوْمِ الْجَمْعِ ذٰلِكَ یَوْمُ التَّغَابُنِ»** — স্মরণ করো সেই মহাদিবসকে, যেদিন আল্লাহ তাআলা পূর্বাপর সমগ্র মানবজাতিকে এক মহাসমাবেশে একত্রিত করবেন; সেই দিনটি হবে ‘ইয়াওমুত তাগাবুন’—অর্থাৎ হার-জিতের আসল রূপ প্রকাশের দিন, পারস্পরিক লাভ ও ক্ষতির দিন! সেদিন কাফিররা বুঝতে পারবে তারা ঈমান হারিয়ে কত মহা ক্ষতিগ্রস্ত হয়েছে, আর মুমিনরা দেখবে সামান্য ঈমান ও নেক আমলের বদলে তারা কত অনন্ত লাভবান হয়েছে।
② **«وَمَنْ یُّؤْمِنْ بِاللّٰهِ وَیَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا یُّكَفِّرْ عَنْهُ سَیِّاٰتِهٖ»** — আর যে ব্যক্তি আল্লাহর প্রতি নিখাদ ঈমান আনবে এবং শরিয়ত মোতাবেক সৎকর্ম সম্পাদন করবে, আল্লাহ তাআলা তার অতীত জীবনের যাবতীয় পাপ ও ত্রুটি মোচন করে দেবেন;
③ **«وَیُدْخِلْهُ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِیْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِیْنَ فِیْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ذٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِیْمُ»** — এবং তাকে চিরসবুজ জান্নাতসমূহে প্রবিষ্ট করাবেন যার পাদদেশে সুরম্য নহরসমূহ প্রবহমান, সেখানে তারা অনন্তকাল বসবাস করবে; মূলত এটিই হলো মহাসাফল্য (আল-ফাওযুল আজিম)!

verses.tf_en:
① **«یَوْمَ یَجْمَعُكُمْ لِیَوْمِ الْجَمْعِ ذٰلِكَ یَوْمُ التَّغَابُنِ»** (The day when He will gather you, on the Day of Collective Assembly – that is the day when the loss of the losers will be laid bare;) — Commemorate with awe that momentous Day when He will assemble all of you together—the Day of Universal Gathering (*Yawm al-Jam'*), when all past and future generations stand before the Lord of the worlds! That is the Day of Mutual Loss and Gain (*Yawm at-Taghabun*)—the Day when the tragic bankruptcy of the disbelievers who traded eternity for transient worldly lusts is exposed, and the supreme triumph of the believers who invested their lives in faith is manifested!;
② **«وَمَنْ یُّؤْمِنْ بِاللّٰهِ وَیَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا یُّكَفِّرْ عَنْهُ سَیِّاٰتِهٖ»** (And whoever believes in Allah and does good deeds, Allah will relieve him of his sins) — And whoever believes sincerely in Allah and performs righteous deeds in accordance with the Sacred Law, Allah will expiate all his sins and absolve him of his past errors;
③ **«وَیُدْخِلْهُ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِیْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِیْنَ فِیْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ذٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِیْمُ»** (And admit him into Gardens beneath which rivers flow, for them to abide in it forever; this is the greatest success.) — And He will usher him into evergreen Gardens of Paradise beneath whose sublime pavilions crystal rivers flow, to abide therein in everlasting bliss; that indeed is the supreme, crowning triumph (*al-Fawz al-'Azeem*)!

① **«مَاۤ اَصَابَ مِنْ مُّصِیْبَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ»** (No misfortune befalls except by Allah’s command;) — No affliction, hardship, illness, or calamity strikes any human being in this mortal realm except by the sovereign leave, decree, and predetermined will (*Qada' and Qadar*) of Allah; nothing occurs by random coincidence or blind fate;
② **«وَمَنْ یُّؤْمِنْ بِاللّٰهِ یَهْدِ قَلْبَهٗ»** (And Allah will guide the heart of whoever accepts faith in Him;) — And whoever maintains steadfast faith in Allah, recognizing that every trial is governed by divine wisdom, and responds with patient endurance (*Sabr*) and contentment (*Rida*), Allah will illuminate, comfort, and guide his heart with serene tranquility and profound certitude;
③ **«وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عَلِیْمٌ»** (And Allah knows all things.) — And Allah possesses all-encompassing, omniscient knowledge of every single thing throughout the creation.

① **«فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ وَاسْمَعُوْا وَاَطِیْعُوْا»** (Therefore fear Allah as much as possible, and heed the commands, and obey,) — Therefore, maintain reverent consciousness and Taqwa of Allah to the utmost limit of your human capacity and ability; listen attentively to His divine verses and prophetic commands, and submit in wholehearted, loyal obedience;
② **«وَاَنْفِقُوْا خَیْرًا لِّاَنْفُسِكُمْ»** (And spend in Allah’s cause, for your own good;) — And spend generously from your lawful earnings in the way of Allah—in charity, jihad, and assisting the destitute—which is infinitely superior and beneficial for the eternal salvation of your own souls;
③ **«وَمَنْ یُّوْقَ شُحَّ نَفْسِهٖ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ»** (And whoever is rescued from the greed of his own soul – is they who will be successful.) — And whoever is preserved by divine grace from the clutching stinginess, avarice, and covetousness of his own ego (*shuhha nafsihi*), it is they alone who are the truly triumphant, prosperous, and successful (*al-Muflihoon*)!
